# Build output. Copying these in would ship a Windows-built bin/ into a linux image and, worse, make the
# layer cache miss on every local build.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Runtime state that must never be baked into an image: a database carrying somebody's library, the logs
# that describe it, and the generated previews.
**/logs/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/thumbnails/
**/backup/
**/ffmpeg/

# The deployment's own configuration, which names real folders on a real NAS. The image ships no
# config.json at all; one is mounted at run time.
config.json
**/config.json.saved-*

# Tooling and editor state. graphify-out/ and .claude/ arrived at the context root when the
# Current/ folder was flattened away; the graph alone is tens of megabytes of generated JSON.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vs/
.claude/
graphify-out/

# Local media used for manual testing - never part of an image.
media/
**/*.user
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation - large, and changing a markdown file should not invalidate the restore layer.
*.md
docs/
tools/
NasBuild.sh
NasBuild.usage.txt

# Except the release notes, which the Host copies into its output as an operator-facing file: excluded,
# the container build fails at publish with MSB3030 while a local build succeeds. It arrives in the
# `COPY . .` layer, after the restore layer, so the reason for the rule above still holds.
!release-notes.md

# Docker's own files.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
